1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:05,005
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,219 --> 00:00:14,180
[Emilia] <i>Kill Madrigal in front of us.</i>

3
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:15,640
[Julio] <i>Shoot the dog!</i>

4
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:17,308
-[gunshot]
-[grunts]

5
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:20,979
[Ivy] <i>I won't taint my hands</i>
<i>just to prove my loyalty!</i>

6
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:23,898
<i>The next time you accuse</i>
<i>your biggest investor,</i>

7
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:29,529
<i>I won't even need to think twice about</i>
<i>siding with your greatest rival.</i>

8
00:00:29,612 --> 00:00:34,659
<i>But for now, my word is as good as gold.</i>

9
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:37,037
[Jepoy] <i>You have</i>
<i>to get out of here, Jepoy.</i>

10
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:41,332
<i>Ivy needs you right now.</i>
<i>I need to endure this for Ivy.</i>

11
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:44,919
[Julio] <i>Since I can't rely on you</i>
<i>when it comes to Miss Aguas,</i>

12
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:49,257
<i>I want you to do something else</i>
<i>to get rid of all my problems.</i>

13
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:51,551
[Diego] <i>Miss Camia,</i>
<i>are you expecting company?</i>

14
00:00:51,634 --> 00:00:53,678
-<i>No.</i>
-[man] <i>There are bodyguards.</i>

15
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:55,305
[Arnaldo] <i>So what? Are you scared?</i>

16
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:57,891
-[thuds]
-[car alarm blares]

17
00:00:57,974 --> 00:01:00,351
-[Diego] <i>Miss Camia, get in.</i>
-[Camia] <i>What's going on?</i>

18
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:04,147
[Ivy] <i>I want you all to be alert</i>
<i>and more careful.</i>

19
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:06,357
<i>I need to save Jepoy.</i>

20
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:07,776
[Diego] <i>I will never forgive myself</i>

21
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:08,902
<i>if something bad happens to you.</i>

22
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:12,614
<i>And I won't forgive myself if Jepoy dies!</i>

23
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:14,616
[Diego] <i>Ivy, I know I can't stop you.</i>

24
00:01:14,699 --> 00:01:15,825
<i>I will help you.</i>

25
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:17,494
[Ivy] <i>I'll find him, Diego.</i>

26
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:19,746
<i>I need to go to the Ardientes.</i>

27
00:01:19,829 --> 00:01:23,291
<i>What did you do to Jepoy?</i>
<i>Is he still alive?</i>

28
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:25,710
<i>Where did you move him?</i>
<i>Where did you take him?</i>

29
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:28,254
<i>You will tell me the name of your boss.</i>

30
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:32,008
<i>If you don't,</i>
<i>I'll drill a hole in your skull</i>

31
00:01:32,091 --> 00:01:34,385
<i>until your brain gushes out!</i>

32
00:01:34,469 --> 00:01:36,387
[Arnaldo] <i>Hello, Mom?</i>
<i>Any news on Madrigal?</i>

33
00:01:36,471 --> 00:01:37,972
<i>Who's his boss? Who does he work for?</i>

34
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:41,893
[Emilia] <i>Did you hear what I said?</i>

35
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:43,353
Madrigal folded.

36
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:45,980
Probably, he couldn't stand the torture.

37
00:01:46,064 --> 00:01:49,442
So, he'll start talking
and he won't try to escape again.

38
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:50,443
Good.

39
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:52,487
I'm coming there.

40
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:54,989
I'll clean up the mess
that Madrigal caused.

41
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:56,199
Don't bother, son.

42
00:01:56,282 --> 00:01:58,284
Your grandpa and I will take care of it.

43
00:01:58,368 --> 00:02:00,829
And this traitor will surely confess.

44
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:05,708
-[Arnaldo] Okay, enjoy.
-All right.

45
00:02:10,171 --> 00:02:13,007
Is that about Madrigal?

46
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:15,885
Yes.

47
00:02:17,011 --> 00:02:19,013
But that traitor is not talking yet.

48
00:02:21,683 --> 00:02:23,643
[sighing] That bastard.

49
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:28,731
That Madrigal is such a bastard.

50
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:31,401
Don't worry.

51
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:39,617
The time is running out
for the traitors of this family.

52
00:02:45,123 --> 00:02:47,792
-Let's go inside?
-Yes, please.

53
00:02:51,004 --> 00:02:53,339
[William] Uh, Congressman and Mrs. Emilia

54
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:56,718
have an emergency to attend to,

55
00:02:56,801 --> 00:02:59,095
but your beloved governor

56
00:02:59,178 --> 00:03:00,597
is ready to listen to all your concerns.

57
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,182
It's better if those Ardientes
don't come back here!

58
00:03:03,266 --> 00:03:05,894
That family is the scourge of this town!

59
00:03:06,436 --> 00:03:07,729
-[men] He's right!
-[William] Hold on.

60
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:09,647
Calm down, everyone.

61
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:11,357
You're just defending your bosses!

62
00:03:11,816 --> 00:03:13,109
Aren't you one of their lapdogs?!

63
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:14,736
-[men] Yeah! He's right!
-[crowd clamoring]

64
00:03:14,819 --> 00:03:17,196
-[William] Hold on, everyone.
-[clamoring]

65
00:03:18,239 --> 00:03:20,158
Please calm down. Have your seats!

66
00:03:21,701 --> 00:03:23,786
Don't start any trouble, everyone!

67
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:25,705
[clamoring]

68
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:29,918
[William] Hold on!

69
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:32,837
What are you doing, huh?!

70
00:03:33,546 --> 00:03:35,506
Why are you just standing around?

71
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:37,425
Give me the mic!

72
00:03:43,431 --> 00:03:44,474
[Arnaldo] Security!

73
00:03:45,016 --> 00:03:46,476
Arrest the agitators!

74
00:03:48,269 --> 00:03:50,146
Mayor Arnaldo is so full
of himself, Governor.

75
00:03:51,231 --> 00:03:55,401
The arrogance of the Ardientes
will bring their demise.

76
00:03:55,818 --> 00:03:58,154
[clamoring]

77
00:03:58,696 --> 00:03:59,739
Let's go.

78
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:07,080
[Arnaldo] To my constituents,
please have your seats.

79
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:11,084
To my constituents…

80
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:15,171
to the loyal supporters of the Ardientes…

81
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:18,675
as long as I'm in power…

82
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:25,473
no traitor or rebel
can defeat the Ardientes!

83
00:04:29,185 --> 00:04:30,520
Viva Ardiente!

84
00:04:30,603 --> 00:04:33,439
-Viva Ardiente!
-Viva Ardiente!

85
00:04:33,523 --> 00:04:36,067
-[townsfolk] Viva Ardiente!
-Viva Ardiente!

86
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:37,694
Viva Ardiente!

87
00:04:46,577 --> 00:04:49,998
[club music playing]

88
00:04:54,085 --> 00:04:57,171
Maybe he wants company. Relax.

89
00:05:01,718 --> 00:05:03,469
Hi, I'm Lovely.

90
00:05:05,763 --> 00:05:07,974
Hi, I'm Honey.

91
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:09,684
Hello.

92
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:24,574
We asked you to handle
the crowd just once…

93
00:05:25,616 --> 00:05:27,201
and then that happened.

94
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:33,708
Anyway, where are the earnings
from the gambling den?

95
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:35,835
We have yet to reach our quota,
Congressman.

96
00:05:35,918 --> 00:05:36,919
[chuckles]

97
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:39,213
Damn it, Alvarez.

98
00:05:39,297 --> 00:05:42,550
You know we need that money
for the next election.

99
00:05:42,633 --> 00:05:46,012
Why don't you take my advice?

100
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:47,805
You know,

101
00:05:48,806 --> 00:05:54,103
just disappear like vapor into thin air

102
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:57,982
and don't come back
until I tell you to do so.

103
00:05:58,441 --> 00:05:59,859
I will never leave.

104
00:06:01,152 --> 00:06:05,907
And let me make this clear
once and for all, Congressman.

105
00:06:06,699 --> 00:06:07,992
I'm not your lapdog.

106
00:06:09,368 --> 00:06:11,996
Be careful with your words, Alvarez.

107
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:15,416
It's me who you're talking to.

108
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:16,876
[chuckles]

109
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:19,754
A typical Ardiente.

110
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:23,758
Always backstabbing one another…

111
00:06:25,176 --> 00:06:28,096
but united when someone
threatens the family.

112
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:33,101
And yet, you're all cowards
when facing criticism.

113
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:39,107
If you only heard the accusations
people have leveled against you.

114
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:41,484
That's the farthest you can go, Governor…

115
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:44,195
unless you want to end up

116
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:48,533
like the ones who dared
to oppose the Ardientes.

117
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:51,702
[foreboding music playing]

118
00:07:04,048 --> 00:07:06,717
Madrigal was my bodyguard for two years.

119
00:07:08,594 --> 00:07:11,013
Sometimes, the people you trust the most

120
00:07:11,097 --> 00:07:12,807
are the ones who betray you.

121
00:07:17,478 --> 00:07:19,814
That's why I believe that loyalty

122
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:22,900
is the most important thing
you can give to someone.

123
00:07:24,152 --> 00:07:26,404
It's even more important than love.

124
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:29,574
You, Mr. Mayor…

125
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:33,578
You've been a wonderful friend to me…

126
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,288
a loyal friend.

127
00:07:36,372 --> 00:07:37,665
But, Miss Aguas…

128
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,418
I don't want to be your friend.

129
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:45,923
I want you ever since.

130
00:07:47,508 --> 00:07:49,844
I want us to be together.

131
00:07:51,345 --> 00:07:56,017
[tense music playing]

132
00:07:59,937 --> 00:08:01,105
Mr. Mayor.

133
00:08:03,816 --> 00:08:07,570
We cannot always get
what we want when we want it.

134
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:16,704
Good night.

135
00:08:27,256 --> 00:08:29,467
[Arnaldo] Oh, Diego!
What are you doing here?

136
00:08:30,718 --> 00:08:33,054
It's none of your business.
I came for Ivy.

137
00:08:33,137 --> 00:08:34,180
But for what?

138
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:37,642
To persuade her to side
with you and Camia?

139
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,854
When will you stop being foolish, huh?!

140
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:46,108
It's never foolish
to protect innocent people

141
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:47,985
from the Ardientes!

142
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:49,779
Oh, really?

143
00:08:50,238 --> 00:08:52,114
And how exactly will you do that, huh?

144
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,241
You can't win.

145
00:08:53,324 --> 00:08:56,244
What's up your sleeve? Your witnesses?

146
00:08:57,119 --> 00:09:00,373
From what I remember, they're all dead.

147
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:05,878
-You bastard!
-[Arnaldo grunting]

148
00:09:06,295 --> 00:09:08,923
-[security] Sir, stop it!
-[Diego] Shame on you!

149
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:11,509
[security] Diego, stop it!

150
00:09:12,134 --> 00:09:13,177
Let go of me!

151
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:16,764
Try to ruin the Ardiente name again,

152
00:09:16,847 --> 00:09:19,308
and your witnesses won't be
the only ones dead.

153
00:09:20,726 --> 00:09:21,727
I'll kill you too.

154
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:25,815
[security] Look out for him.

155
00:09:25,898 --> 00:09:27,108
Stop!

156
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:42,331
Stop it! What are you doing here, huh?!

157
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:43,749
You! Get out!

158
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:45,418
Out!

159
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:47,670
Leave my property.

160
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:50,214
And spare me from your plans with Camia

161
00:09:50,298 --> 00:09:54,385
because I don't want to be involved
with either of you!

162
00:09:54,468 --> 00:09:55,386
Do you understand?!

163
00:10:02,059 --> 00:10:03,102
Out!

164
00:10:04,353 --> 00:10:05,563
Now!

165
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,402
Mr. Mayor, what happened?

166
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:12,945
Are you okay?

167
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:15,489
Yeah, I'm okay.

168
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:17,408
I can't believe him.

169
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:22,455
Thank you.

170
00:10:30,171 --> 00:10:33,049
[Camia] Check all the gates,
doors, and windows.

171
00:10:33,132 --> 00:10:36,385
Make sure that Raul
can't enter this house.

172
00:10:36,469 --> 00:10:37,386
[security] Yes, ma'am.

173
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:41,223
Camia, we just moved in.

174
00:10:41,599 --> 00:10:44,352
I'm sure Raul won't bother us here.

175
00:10:45,353 --> 00:10:49,482
Carlotta, Raul is lying.

176
00:10:50,358 --> 00:10:52,818
He can't possibly care about my safety.

177
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:57,865
He locked me up for so long.
That man is heartless.

178
00:10:57,948 --> 00:11:00,159
[Carlotta] But, what if…

179
00:11:01,952 --> 00:11:05,831
he's telling the truth about saving you?

180
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:10,169
If that's the case, I'll thank him.

181
00:11:11,462 --> 00:11:16,133
But I know why he's doing this,
to regain my trust.

182
00:11:17,176 --> 00:11:19,261
But I won't make the same mistake.

183
00:11:34,402 --> 00:11:35,611
Aha!

184
00:11:37,113 --> 00:11:40,157
So, this is what the Ardientes
have been hiding.

185
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:44,578
This is why they left the charity event…

186
00:11:45,329 --> 00:11:46,914
and made me look like an idiot.

187
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:51,502
So, who are you?

188
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:56,090
How did you betray the Ardientes?

189
00:11:57,508 --> 00:11:58,926
Did they treat you horribly?

190
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:06,183
Well, the Ardientes are really arrogant,

191
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:07,893
so I can't blame you.

192
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,941
[man] Governor,
here's the collected money.

193
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:16,193
Ah!

194
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:17,695
Very good.

195
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,363
[chuckling]

196
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:23,117
Go ahead, Ardientes…

197
00:12:24,201 --> 00:12:26,704
-Keep on belittling me.
-[man chuckles]

198
00:12:27,413 --> 00:12:30,666
I'll drain all your wealth.

199
00:12:31,709 --> 00:12:33,085
[laughs]

200
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:34,211
Put it back there.

201
00:12:35,504 --> 00:12:36,422
[chuckles]

202
00:12:45,055 --> 00:12:46,807
-[all] Cheers.
-Shot!

203
00:12:49,101 --> 00:12:51,604
[Raul] Wait, I forgot the salt.

204
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:54,106
Let me put it here.

205
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:56,525
[Honey] Go, go, go!

206
00:12:56,609 --> 00:13:00,404
[Natalie] Excuse me. Mind if I join you?

207
00:13:04,241 --> 00:13:05,493
In the flesh.

208
00:13:06,827 --> 00:13:07,870
Natalie?

209
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:13,125
[Natalie] Okay, ladies, playtime is over.

210
00:13:13,834 --> 00:13:14,877
Get out.

211
00:13:17,129 --> 00:13:18,797
-I said, get out.
-[Raul] Later, girls.

212
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:23,928
[Raul chuckles]

213
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:27,223
Hmm!

214
00:13:27,848 --> 00:13:28,891
What are we having?

215
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:42,363
Mr. Mayor, we need to do this
so you won't get bruises.

216
00:13:50,579 --> 00:13:51,830
[Arnaldo] I can take care of it.

217
00:13:53,457 --> 00:13:55,751
But thanks for getting rid
of that bastard.

218
00:13:57,962 --> 00:14:01,257
It's his fault for storming here.

219
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:06,929
[Arnaldo] You know what,
you've always been loyal to me.

220
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:10,224
It feels like…

221
00:14:12,101 --> 00:14:13,727
there's this thing between us.

222
00:14:15,729 --> 00:14:16,730
And I know…

223
00:14:18,065 --> 00:14:19,149
I'm not the only one…

224
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:23,529
who feels the same way.

225
00:14:25,531 --> 00:14:26,615
So I was thinking…

226
00:14:30,411 --> 00:14:34,415
why don't we make this official?

227
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:38,127
I mean, think about it.

228
00:14:39,169 --> 00:14:42,214
No one can stop us.

229
00:14:42,965 --> 00:14:45,926
Natalie is gone, and we're both single.

230
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:49,972
In my opinion, I think it's time for us

231
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:51,682
to pick up where we left off.

232
00:14:57,438 --> 00:15:00,774
Arnaldo, I'll be right back.

233
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:03,235
Miss Aguas.

234
00:15:07,281 --> 00:15:08,449
Stay.

235
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:34,934
Well, whatever that is…

236
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:37,728
I still want you.

237
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:43,984
You said you can take care of yourself.

238
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:48,864
Good night, Mr. Mayor.

239
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:16,016
Well, I went to Paris,
and I went to Berlin.

240
00:16:16,725 --> 00:16:19,603
And Berlin somehow became a favorite.

241
00:16:20,437 --> 00:16:24,733
I loved it so much,
I almost didn't come back.

242
00:16:25,317 --> 00:16:27,987
That's the thing. Why did you come back?

243
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:31,323
Everyone comes back for a reason.

244
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:33,909
Until now,

245
00:16:34,702 --> 00:16:39,081
I ponder how my dad died so suddenly.

246
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:41,458
You know, those kinds of death…

247
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:44,545
It's not by accident.

248
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:51,093
I know someone had him killed,
and I want to know who it is.

249
00:16:52,261 --> 00:16:54,013
But let's not talk about that now.

250
00:16:54,596 --> 00:16:55,556
You know what?

251
00:16:55,639 --> 00:16:57,891
You're actually looking a lot hotter

252
00:16:57,975 --> 00:17:03,105
than I remember, Uncle Raul.
Or should I call you Raul?

253
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:06,817
In fact, you're looking a lot hotter

254
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:08,110
than someone I know.

255
00:17:09,653 --> 00:17:13,866
Someone named Arnaldo, perhaps?

256
00:17:16,994 --> 00:17:19,079
I'm actually glad
that I came here tonight.

257
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:21,540
I think I'll come here more often now.

258
00:17:22,416 --> 00:17:24,334
Really? [chuckles]

259
00:17:25,586 --> 00:17:26,670
Cheers.

260
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:30,841
[William] Well, look at this.

261
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:35,637
You have the governor as your babysitter.

262
00:17:38,223 --> 00:17:40,225
Tell me who your boss is…

263
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:45,230
so I could earn a brownie point
from Julio.

264
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:53,197
His grandson, Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente…

265
00:17:55,532 --> 00:17:59,411
a charismatic leader
and idol of the masses…

266
00:18:00,954 --> 00:18:04,625
and has a beautiful woman by his side.

267
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:10,547
But you know…

268
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:17,554
I'm more than satisfied
to get a taste of that woman.

269
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:21,016
Just for once…

270
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:27,064
I get to see how it feels
to be Arnaldo Ardiente.

271
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:33,028
[line ringing]

272
00:18:33,112 --> 00:18:34,196
Benjie.

273
00:18:35,405 --> 00:18:37,783
Find out where Ivy Aguas lives.

274
00:18:38,742 --> 00:18:39,785
Yeah.

275
00:18:40,994 --> 00:18:42,246
Bring her to me.

276
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:53,048
Alvarez is testing my patience.

277
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:55,926
That's why I tasked him
to look after Madrigal.

278
00:18:57,719 --> 00:18:58,720
[sighs]

279
00:19:01,557 --> 00:19:02,599
Oh!

280
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:05,352
-Good morning, Miss Aguas!
-[Ivy] Good morning.

281
00:19:06,395 --> 00:19:08,021
[Julio] You're a sight for sore eyes.

282
00:19:08,564 --> 00:19:10,482
I didn't know you were
joining us for breakfast.

283
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:14,403
I came to see Mr. Mayor, Congressman.

284
00:19:14,736 --> 00:19:15,779
Good morning.

285
00:19:16,905 --> 00:19:19,032
-I have something for you.
-[Arnaldo] Well, thank you.

286
00:19:19,408 --> 00:19:21,201
Please, sit down.

287
00:19:24,454 --> 00:19:27,332
I had an altercation with
everyone's favorite bastard,

288
00:19:27,666 --> 00:19:29,126
and Ivy took care of me.

289
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:35,424
Well, you better make sure
that Diego had it worse.

290
00:19:36,216 --> 00:19:37,926
You have nothing to worry about, Grandpa.

291
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:41,096
And also, I'll be gracing
an opening of a museum

292
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:42,139
in Manila.

293
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:43,265
Ivy's gonna be my date.

294
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:46,685
Date?

295
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:50,939
Um…

296
00:19:51,607 --> 00:19:55,194
Does this mean Natalie is ancient history?

297
00:19:55,694 --> 00:19:56,695
[chuckles]

298
00:19:57,696 --> 00:19:59,823
Well, I think it's better
not to talk about her…

299
00:20:00,532 --> 00:20:03,785
especially if I crowned Ivy
my future first lady.

300
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:10,083
Affairs of the heart, I leave to you.

301
00:20:11,501 --> 00:20:13,337
Future first lady?

302
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:16,131
Can't I be your future date first?

303
00:20:23,013 --> 00:20:25,182
Please, have some coffee or tea.

304
00:20:26,308 --> 00:20:27,351
Thank you.

305
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:37,152
[Julio] Madrigal, I give you two choices.

306
00:20:38,695 --> 00:20:39,738
I give you a minute.

307
00:20:40,906 --> 00:20:45,953
Tell me what I wanna hear, or you die.

308
00:20:48,497 --> 00:20:52,042
In one minute, remember.

309
00:20:53,835 --> 00:20:57,631
So, are you going to spill the beans, huh?

310
00:21:01,718 --> 00:21:03,470
Cover him now.

311
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:07,057
-Go.
-[spurting]

312
00:21:07,557 --> 00:21:13,522
[Julio] Ten, nine, eight, seven, six,

313
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:15,524
five…

314
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:18,151
[coughing]

315
00:21:19,861 --> 00:21:22,990
[gasping]

316
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:25,200
Madrigal.

317
00:21:25,826 --> 00:21:28,578
Madrigal! Can you hear me?!

318
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:34,293
This is your last chance.
I'll count to 10.

319
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:36,044
If you still don't confess…

320
00:21:37,838 --> 00:21:44,177
this water and piece of cloth
will drown you to death!

321
00:21:46,346 --> 00:21:48,348
Now just to be sure.

322
00:21:50,726 --> 00:21:51,852
I'll count to 10.

323
00:21:52,769 --> 00:21:58,275
Ten, nine, eight, seven,

324
00:21:59,234 --> 00:22:02,654
six, five… Last chance!

325
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:09,036
Four, three, two, one! Drown him!

326
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:12,122
[spurting]

327
00:22:12,205 --> 00:22:13,999
-[Jepoy mumbling]
-What was that?

328
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:16,126
Take it off.

329
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:19,296
-[stuttering] I'm going to talk!
-[Julio] What?

330
00:22:19,671 --> 00:22:21,757
-I'm going to talk.
-[Julio] Good!

331
00:22:23,592 --> 00:22:25,218
Give me the answer I want.

332
00:22:26,762 --> 00:22:28,805
Who's your boss?

333
00:22:28,889 --> 00:22:31,224
[Jepoy coughing]

334
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:36,063
[phone ringing]

335
00:22:37,898 --> 00:22:39,274
Yes, Mr. Mayor?

336
00:22:39,357 --> 00:22:40,442
Hello, Miss Aguas.

337
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:44,321
Yes, I'm sorry. I'm afraid
we have to cancel our date.

338
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:46,907
The congressman and Mom need me here.

339
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:48,408
<i>Madrigal is finally talking.</i>

340
00:22:52,788 --> 00:22:54,498
Who is he working for?

341
00:23:04,132 --> 00:23:05,884
[Julio] Give me the answer I want.

342
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:09,888
[gasping] The governor. The governor.

343
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:14,267
-Who?
-Alvarez!

344
00:23:14,351 --> 00:23:20,190
[tense music playing]

345
00:23:25,278 --> 00:23:28,406
[Carlotta] Ivy, I already
asked Diego to come down.

346
00:23:29,574 --> 00:23:30,659
Thank you.

347
00:23:32,202 --> 00:23:33,787
Ivy, I'm sorry. I'm just worried,

348
00:23:33,870 --> 00:23:35,038
so I went to you.

349
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:36,790
-I didn't know Arnaldo--
-Diego…

350
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:39,709
I should be the one to apologize.

351
00:23:41,002 --> 00:23:44,881
I'm sorry for sending you away last night.

352
00:23:45,841 --> 00:23:49,553
You know that I need information
to save Jepoy.

353
00:23:50,178 --> 00:23:52,848
But, Ivy, I don't want you
playing with fire.

354
00:23:54,099 --> 00:23:56,101
I won't get burned in the game.

355
00:23:56,977 --> 00:23:57,978
Can't you just…

356
00:23:59,229 --> 00:24:01,106
Can we first think this through?

357
00:24:02,566 --> 00:24:03,733
We can't, Diego.

358
00:24:05,277 --> 00:24:06,403
I can't stop.

359
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:08,572
Many things happened to the Ardientes.

360
00:24:08,655 --> 00:24:10,740
They've been exposed and sued,

361
00:24:10,824 --> 00:24:12,784
but they're still free.

362
00:24:12,868 --> 00:24:14,411
They still have Jepoy.

363
00:24:16,037 --> 00:24:17,873
I can't stop now.

364
00:24:18,623 --> 00:24:20,917
Because in every minute I waste,

365
00:24:21,001 --> 00:24:23,587
the Ardientes are taking a step forward.

366
00:24:27,507 --> 00:24:29,593
The war has just begun, Diego.

367
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:35,056
Ivy's war has just begun.

368
00:24:37,392 --> 00:24:39,603
That's why I need
to stay close to Arnaldo…

369
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:43,523
so I'll know the plans of the Ardientes.

370
00:24:44,524 --> 00:24:48,653
We will win this war,
and we will save Jepoy.

371
00:24:55,952 --> 00:24:57,329
[Diego] If you're going to fight…

372
00:24:57,829 --> 00:24:58,872
then I'll fight too.

373
00:25:00,415 --> 00:25:02,292
As long as the Ardientes are in power,

374
00:25:02,375 --> 00:25:03,501
they can't be brought down.

375
00:25:04,211 --> 00:25:06,213
Someone should fight them head-on.

376
00:25:07,631 --> 00:25:08,882
What do you mean?

377
00:25:09,549 --> 00:25:11,384
I will run for governor.

378
00:25:13,386 --> 00:25:15,305
Ivy, times have changed.

379
00:25:15,805 --> 00:25:18,391
The people aren't ignorant like before.

380
00:25:18,892 --> 00:25:20,894
Many are aware of the cruelty
of the Ardientes.

381
00:25:20,977 --> 00:25:23,980
And now, I will lead them towards change.

382
00:25:25,690 --> 00:25:29,903
I will do everything
in my power to help you win.

383
00:25:32,239 --> 00:25:34,366
And bring downfall to the Ardientes.

384
00:25:36,159 --> 00:25:38,203
For a new Poblacion Ardiente.

385
00:25:52,801 --> 00:25:53,885
[Arnaldo] Grandpa.

386
00:25:54,427 --> 00:25:55,971
-[man grunting]
-Speak up!

387
00:25:56,972 --> 00:25:58,223
Congressman.

388
00:25:59,432 --> 00:26:01,518
The governor has been holding
a grudge against you.

389
00:26:02,102 --> 00:26:04,271
We used hear him say

390
00:26:04,354 --> 00:26:06,356
that he's enduring all your hurtful words

391
00:26:06,439 --> 00:26:08,733
while he drains your money.

392
00:26:11,069 --> 00:26:14,197
Then show me the money.

393
00:26:15,782 --> 00:26:20,745
Return every cent
that Alvarez stole from me.

394
00:26:21,454 --> 00:26:23,748
Governor Alvarez has it all, Congressman.

395
00:26:29,629 --> 00:26:30,714
Arnaldo.

396
00:26:33,591 --> 00:26:34,968
You know what to do.

397
00:26:38,388 --> 00:26:41,933
Have mercy, Congressman!
I already told the truth!

398
00:26:42,017 --> 00:26:43,977
Please have mercy! I have a family!

399
00:26:50,483 --> 00:26:55,739
Jepoy wouldn't point Alvarez
without a reason.

400
00:26:56,197 --> 00:26:57,240
If that's the case…

401
00:26:59,034 --> 00:27:01,286
we need to find out why he chose Alvarez.

402
00:27:02,704 --> 00:27:03,496
Here, look at this.

403
00:27:15,884 --> 00:27:19,179
Governor William Alvarez
has very good credentials,

404
00:27:19,262 --> 00:27:23,308
and yet he's being pushed around
by the Ardientes.

405
00:27:31,483 --> 00:27:35,487
Alvarez manages the largest
charity institution in Ardiente.

406
00:27:36,154 --> 00:27:40,742
Many corrupt officials
use charity institutions

407
00:27:40,825 --> 00:27:43,620
to hide their ill-gotten wealth.

408
00:27:47,207 --> 00:27:53,421
Does Alvarez have a hidden
grudge against the Ardientes?

409
00:27:53,505 --> 00:27:56,674
That's why he's stealing from them.

410
00:27:57,717 --> 00:27:59,094
I'll look for Alvarez.

411
00:27:59,177 --> 00:28:02,555
Arnaldo also needs
to know this information.

412
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:09,604
Governor Alvarez.

413
00:28:20,115 --> 00:28:23,284
[Arnaldo] The good news
is Madrigal was right.

414
00:28:24,744 --> 00:28:27,747
Alvarez has been stealing money
from my family.

415
00:28:28,081 --> 00:28:31,543
But the bad news is that Alvarez is gone…

416
00:28:32,085 --> 00:28:34,754
-<i>along with the stolen money.</i>
-[maid screaming]

417
00:28:35,505 --> 00:28:37,298
<i>Where is your boss? Where is Alvarez?</i>

418
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:39,676
<i>-I don't know, sir.</i>
<i>-Search upstairs.</i>

419
00:28:39,759 --> 00:28:41,636
[goon 1] <i>Stay right there!</i>

420
00:28:48,143 --> 00:28:49,477
[goon 2] <i>Sir, the vault is empty.</i>

421
00:28:52,814 --> 00:28:55,525
[phone ringing]

422
00:28:56,735 --> 00:28:57,819
<i>Negative.</i>

423
00:28:57,902 --> 00:29:00,238
<i>Alvarez is not here,</i>
<i>and neither is our money.</i>

424
00:29:08,496 --> 00:29:11,040
[Ivy] <i>So, Madrigal's confession</i>
<i>was useless.</i>

425
00:29:13,418 --> 00:29:14,294
Unfortunately.

426
00:29:15,920 --> 00:29:17,714
Then, what's next for Madrigal?

427
00:29:19,257 --> 00:29:23,094
You know what we do to people
or things that are useless…

428
00:29:24,387 --> 00:29:25,972
they get disposed of.

429
00:29:55,043 --> 00:29:56,336
[Ivy] <i>You know, Mr. Mayor…</i>

430
00:29:56,753 --> 00:30:01,758
I have a feeling
that you'll still need Madrigal.

431
00:30:03,426 --> 00:30:04,469
You know why?

432
00:30:05,845 --> 00:30:09,307
I did my own research, and look at this.

433
00:30:12,602 --> 00:30:15,647
Governor Alvarez isn't just a thief.

434
00:30:15,730 --> 00:30:18,817
Governor Alvarez is also
funneling government funds

435
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:21,694
into his charity institution.

436
00:30:22,695 --> 00:30:24,280
You know what that means?

437
00:30:24,864 --> 00:30:27,742
You can sue Governor Alvarez,

438
00:30:28,326 --> 00:30:33,706
and Madrigal will be
your number one witness.

439
00:30:35,416 --> 00:30:36,709
Okay, go on.

440
00:30:40,797 --> 00:30:44,843
[phone ringing]

441
00:30:47,178 --> 00:30:48,388
Hello?

442
00:30:48,471 --> 00:30:49,514
[Diego] <i>Ivy.</i>

443
00:30:51,224 --> 00:30:53,977
I went to a house
featured in an online article.

444
00:30:54,060 --> 00:30:55,144
It's confirmed.

445
00:30:55,228 --> 00:30:57,397
This is the rest house
of Alvarez in Tagaytay.

446
00:31:00,149 --> 00:31:02,026
Okay, thank you.

447
00:31:05,280 --> 00:31:06,114
[Arnaldo] <i>Who was that?</i>

448
00:31:09,492 --> 00:31:11,703
My own source of intelligence.

449
00:31:16,583 --> 00:31:17,959
Well, Mr. Mayor…

450
00:31:23,882 --> 00:31:24,799
like what I said…

451
00:31:28,052 --> 00:31:30,722
sue Governor Alvarez…

452
00:31:32,265 --> 00:31:34,809
and I'll tell you where he is.

453
00:31:36,394 --> 00:31:37,478
And Madrigal?

454
00:31:40,106 --> 00:31:44,027
He's going to be your number one witness.

455
00:31:48,615 --> 00:31:49,657
Can I join you?

456
00:31:51,242 --> 00:31:52,160
Please.

457
00:32:04,964 --> 00:32:07,300
You are of no use now, Madrigal.

458
00:32:09,719 --> 00:32:10,720
<i>Adios.</i>

459
00:32:12,055 --> 00:32:13,097
Make him kneel.

460
00:32:16,935 --> 00:32:17,977
Well…

461
00:32:18,686 --> 00:32:19,938
-[cocks gun]
-Well, do it!

462
00:32:23,358 --> 00:32:24,400
Lower your guns.

463
00:32:27,236 --> 00:32:29,197
We can't kill him right now.

464
00:32:31,783 --> 00:32:33,618
And why is that?

465
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:38,122
We'll use him as a witness against Alvarez

466
00:32:38,206 --> 00:32:40,875
for stealing government funds.

467
00:32:40,959 --> 00:32:44,545
[Julio] And how the hell
are we going to do that?!

468
00:32:44,629 --> 00:32:46,589
We don't even know where he is.

469
00:32:46,673 --> 00:32:49,467
Well, good thing I have an idea
about his whereabouts.

470
00:32:55,139 --> 00:32:56,683
No problem, Mr. Mayor.

471
00:32:59,060 --> 00:33:00,061
Good.

472
00:33:08,903 --> 00:33:11,406
[Ivy] <i>They can't kill you, Jepoy,</i>

473
00:33:11,489 --> 00:33:13,700
<i>because I won't let them.</i>

474
00:33:28,464 --> 00:33:33,136
<i>I'll do everything in my power</i>
<i>just to keep you alive.</i>

475
00:33:39,684 --> 00:33:41,561
[Emilia] This can't be
happening, Aunt Claire.

476
00:33:41,644 --> 00:33:43,604
We have to do something about it.

477
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:46,858
Don't worry, Emilia. I'll help you.

478
00:33:47,316 --> 00:33:49,861
Arnaldo will eventually return
to his senses.

479
00:33:51,195 --> 00:33:53,406
Well, what are you two doing?

480
00:33:55,324 --> 00:33:58,536
-Plotting my murder?
-Of course not, Papa.

481
00:33:59,662 --> 00:34:02,415
I'm worried about Arnaldo and Ivy.

482
00:34:02,749 --> 00:34:03,833
What about them?

483
00:34:05,251 --> 00:34:09,380
You shouldn't despise something
just because you cannot have it.

484
00:34:10,339 --> 00:34:13,217
But, Papa, future First Lady?

485
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:17,805
You know, I must admit before,
I wanted Ivy for Arnaldo

486
00:34:17,889 --> 00:34:19,015
because of her money.

487
00:34:19,098 --> 00:34:20,850
But that was before, Papa.

488
00:34:20,933 --> 00:34:24,687
Now, loyalty is more important
to me than money.

489
00:34:25,688 --> 00:34:28,357
Emilia, I trust your son.

490
00:34:28,816 --> 00:34:32,570
And besides, if Ivy Aguas
is truly the enemy…

491
00:34:33,529 --> 00:34:37,075
then we need to have her by our side.

492
00:34:38,367 --> 00:34:41,037
To quote my favorite philosopher…

493
00:34:41,704 --> 00:34:42,705
"To win the war,

494
00:34:44,248 --> 00:34:49,087
keep your friends close
and your enemies closer."

495
00:34:53,049 --> 00:34:54,884
You two should really learn…

496
00:34:56,636 --> 00:34:58,679
instead of gossiping all the time.

497
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:04,560
That's what you think, Julio.

498
00:35:05,520 --> 00:35:06,687
[Julio scoffs]

499
00:35:06,771 --> 00:35:08,815
I heard you, Claire!

500
00:35:14,737 --> 00:35:18,950
[tense music]

501
00:35:26,666 --> 00:35:27,667
[suppressed gunshot]

502
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:32,130
[suppressed gunshots]

503
00:35:41,139 --> 00:35:43,599
-Mayor!
-How's life, Governor?

504
00:35:43,683 --> 00:35:44,684
What's up?

505
00:35:46,561 --> 00:35:49,397
Good thing I caught up with you
before you escaped your crimes.

506
00:35:49,480 --> 00:35:50,690
Crimes?

507
00:35:51,774 --> 00:35:54,485
Against who? The Ardientes?

508
00:35:54,861 --> 00:35:57,738
If you're talking about
the spare change I took,

509
00:35:57,822 --> 00:36:02,285
that's nothing compared
to your ill-gotten wealth.

510
00:36:03,286 --> 00:36:04,745
Such hurtful words.

511
00:36:10,626 --> 00:36:13,045
Tell it to the Congressman, Governor.

512
00:36:19,218 --> 00:36:20,261
All right, then.

513
00:36:21,721 --> 00:36:23,181
I better get going, Mayor.

514
00:36:25,349 --> 00:36:26,350
What's wrong?

515
00:36:26,434 --> 00:36:28,436
Do it. Pull the trigger.

516
00:36:29,562 --> 00:36:32,940
Don't think that I won't pull the trigger

517
00:36:33,399 --> 00:36:35,234
for your beloved mayor!

518
00:36:36,068 --> 00:36:38,863
Come on! Shoot me!

519
00:36:39,363 --> 00:36:40,406
[gunshot]

520
00:36:42,992 --> 00:36:44,076
[Arnaldo] After him!

521
00:37:00,426 --> 00:37:02,094
<i>More than 10 million pesos</i>

522
00:37:02,178 --> 00:37:05,806
<i>were retrieved by Mayor Arnaldo Torillo</i>

523
00:37:05,890 --> 00:37:09,685
<i>among the belongings</i>
<i>of Governor Alvarez earlier today.</i>

524
00:37:09,769 --> 00:37:12,939
<i>However, the governor managed</i>
<i>to escape from the scene.</i>

525
00:37:13,022 --> 00:37:15,524
<i>A manhunt operation is underway</i>

526
00:37:15,608 --> 00:37:18,694
<i>for him to face</i>
<i>his graft and corruption raps.</i>

527
00:37:20,488 --> 00:37:22,865
Now that they got
what they wanted from Alvarez,

528
00:37:22,949 --> 00:37:25,368
when will they release Jepoy?

529
00:37:25,451 --> 00:37:26,994
Why are they still keeping him?

530
00:37:27,370 --> 00:37:28,371
Lily…

531
00:37:28,454 --> 00:37:32,416
This wasn't supposed to happen.
We have to put an end to this.

532
00:37:32,500 --> 00:37:36,003
Many were affected by this,
like Governor Alvarez,

533
00:37:36,087 --> 00:37:38,297
-as well as--
-[Camia] Alvarez is a criminal.

534
00:37:38,381 --> 00:37:40,967
He has to answer
not just to the Ardientes,

535
00:37:41,050 --> 00:37:42,385
but to the people as well.

536
00:37:42,468 --> 00:37:44,095
But what about Jepoy?

537
00:37:44,804 --> 00:37:46,222
What about Jepoy?

538
00:37:46,305 --> 00:37:48,641
He's still keeping my secrets.

539
00:37:49,934 --> 00:37:52,019
I don't know what the Ardientes
are doing to him.

540
00:37:52,103 --> 00:37:53,437
How long can he fight?

541
00:37:53,521 --> 00:37:55,731
How long are they going to torture him?

542
00:37:55,815 --> 00:37:58,609
[Camia] Lily, Jepoy zeroed in on Alvarez

543
00:37:58,693 --> 00:38:00,861
because it's his way of fighting back.

544
00:38:02,029 --> 00:38:04,198
I know you're feeling guilty,

545
00:38:04,282 --> 00:38:06,534
but for now, it's better that Alvarez

546
00:38:06,617 --> 00:38:09,912
is the one being targeted, not you.

547
00:38:21,716 --> 00:38:23,843
Go on. Release him.

548
00:38:30,391 --> 00:38:32,351
-[Julio whoops]
-[grunting]

549
00:38:32,435 --> 00:38:34,520
Easy, boy. Easy.

550
00:38:35,521 --> 00:38:38,691
You know what, Madrigal? You were right.

551
00:38:39,358 --> 00:38:41,235
You were telling me the truth.

552
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:46,449
I finally got the money
that Alvarez stole from me.

553
00:38:48,409 --> 00:38:49,452
Just one question.

554
00:38:50,453 --> 00:38:52,371
I'm just wondering…

555
00:38:54,415 --> 00:38:57,585
How did he become your boss?

556
00:39:02,715 --> 00:39:03,966
He's not my boss.

557
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:11,682
I suspected him to be a traitor
to the Ardiente family.

558
00:39:13,225 --> 00:39:16,062
-That's why I bugged him.
-[chuckles]

559
00:39:17,605 --> 00:39:21,692
[Julio] Why didn't you tell us
immediately, huh?

560
00:39:22,234 --> 00:39:24,653
Why did you choose to be tortured

561
00:39:24,737 --> 00:39:27,490
and experience
all this pain and suffering?

562
00:39:27,865 --> 00:39:30,326
You know, this is
a big question mark in my head.

563
00:39:30,409 --> 00:39:32,703
-Why?
-Because it's useless.

564
00:39:33,371 --> 00:39:34,288
Huh?

565
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:36,290
Because Ardientes have this nature…

566
00:39:38,876 --> 00:39:42,380
you're all bloodthirsty to kill.

567
00:39:43,297 --> 00:39:45,466
[Jepoy breathing deeply]

568
00:39:45,549 --> 00:39:51,305
Now, let's not get
over ourselves, Madrigal.

569
00:39:52,139 --> 00:39:55,142
You helped me, I'll give you that.

570
00:39:55,226 --> 00:39:57,853
But just because you helped me

571
00:39:58,979 --> 00:40:02,775
doesn't mean you can judge me!

572
00:40:03,818 --> 00:40:05,152
You don't know me!

573
00:40:06,362 --> 00:40:08,197
You don't know me, Madrigal!

574
00:40:09,532 --> 00:40:12,952
But still, I thank you…

575
00:40:14,245 --> 00:40:17,456
because you did that to protect my family.

576
00:40:19,250 --> 00:40:20,334
I'm loyal to you.

577
00:40:23,629 --> 00:40:24,755
I proved that already.

578
00:40:28,008 --> 00:40:29,427
So when will you release me?

579
00:40:30,428 --> 00:40:33,347
I would like to reward you, Madrigal.

580
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:35,683
I really would!

581
00:40:37,601 --> 00:40:40,020
But not just yet.

582
00:40:42,690 --> 00:40:44,233
Not yet.

583
00:40:46,944 --> 00:40:49,905
Uh… Excuse me, dear.
I'll just go upstairs.

584
00:40:50,281 --> 00:40:51,323
Okay, Mom.

585
00:40:54,076 --> 00:40:55,953
Diego, are you sure you weren't followed?

586
00:40:56,036 --> 00:40:58,664
I'm sure. My investigation went smoothly.

587
00:40:59,081 --> 00:41:01,917
Thank you so much for finding Alvarez.

588
00:41:03,586 --> 00:41:08,007
That really helped us to save Jepoy.

589
00:41:08,549 --> 00:41:10,593
But, Diego, I hope that was the last.

590
00:41:12,970 --> 00:41:14,305
What do you mean?

591
00:41:15,097 --> 00:41:17,308
Too many people are getting involved

592
00:41:17,391 --> 00:41:19,101
and getting hurt in my plans.

593
00:41:19,685 --> 00:41:21,770
I don't want you to also get into trouble.

594
00:41:23,189 --> 00:41:24,565
Ivy, I know you feel guilty

595
00:41:24,648 --> 00:41:27,234
for what happened to Alvarez and Jepoy.

596
00:41:27,735 --> 00:41:28,777
But it's me, Ivy.

597
00:41:29,153 --> 00:41:30,946
We were there for each other
since childhood.

598
00:41:31,030 --> 00:41:32,031
What are you afraid of?

599
00:41:32,114 --> 00:41:34,283
I'm scared that you might also get caught.

600
00:41:34,366 --> 00:41:37,328
If they catch you,
they might torture you too.

601
00:41:37,411 --> 00:41:40,414
I can't forgive myself
if that happens, Diego.

602
00:41:53,177 --> 00:41:54,970
Ivy, I want you to trust me.

603
00:41:55,054 --> 00:41:56,764
Let me protect you

604
00:41:56,847 --> 00:41:59,725
because there's nothing
I wouldn't do for you.

605
00:42:29,964 --> 00:42:31,423
[Emilia] Hear me out, Aunt Claire.

606
00:42:31,507 --> 00:42:35,010
That Alvarez is losing
his family's wealth,

607
00:42:35,094 --> 00:42:36,845
became a gambling addict,

608
00:42:36,929 --> 00:42:39,890
and now stole from our family.

609
00:42:40,641 --> 00:42:42,393
That only means one thing, Auntie.

610
00:42:43,018 --> 00:42:46,647
Alvarez is out, and Emilia is so in!

611
00:42:47,940 --> 00:42:49,149
Emilia, darling.

612
00:42:50,276 --> 00:42:52,987
How sure are you
that you will be reinstated

613
00:42:53,070 --> 00:42:54,780
by your dad as governor?

614
00:42:54,863 --> 00:42:57,199
Auntie, I won't wait for that anymore.

615
00:42:57,283 --> 00:42:58,909
I'll reinstate myself.

616
00:43:00,452 --> 00:43:01,495
[Raul] Emilia.

617
00:43:02,288 --> 00:43:03,414
Congratulations.

618
00:43:03,789 --> 00:43:06,375
I heard that you'll be back in office.

619
00:43:06,458 --> 00:43:09,086
Honestly, you're really meant for that

620
00:43:09,169 --> 00:43:12,256
because you're the queen of this town.

621
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:15,301
Raul, thank you for the kind words.

622
00:43:15,384 --> 00:43:18,554
But, you'll soon be
the king of this town too.

623
00:43:19,346 --> 00:43:21,640
Me as the king? I doubt it.

624
00:43:22,641 --> 00:43:26,478
Congressman Julio and Arnaldo
are the only kings here.

625
00:43:26,562 --> 00:43:29,982
As for me, let's just say
that I'm an escort.

626
00:43:30,065 --> 00:43:31,233
But at least…

627
00:43:31,900 --> 00:43:35,613
I'm the escort of
Queen Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.

628
00:43:36,488 --> 00:43:38,699
You know, Raul,
I know you're being sarcastic,

629
00:43:38,782 --> 00:43:41,285
but I'll take you seriously for now.

630
00:43:44,455 --> 00:43:45,623
All right, I'll go ahead.

631
00:43:49,043 --> 00:43:50,085
Bye.

632
00:43:57,593 --> 00:43:59,553
You're falling for his smooth talks again.

633
00:43:59,637 --> 00:44:02,473
Auntie, Raul has changed a lot, right?

634
00:44:03,724 --> 00:44:06,101
-What if he hasn't?
-I'd like to see him try.

635
00:44:06,185 --> 00:44:09,438
That's if he wants to have more
of his mistresses killed.

636
00:44:11,398 --> 00:44:13,359
Governor Emilia is back.

637
00:44:23,702 --> 00:44:27,706
I've been waiting all night.
I thought you weren't coming.

638
00:44:27,790 --> 00:44:30,167
I'm sorry. I couldn't find the right time.

639
00:44:30,834 --> 00:44:32,461
Many things happened at the house.

640
00:44:34,088 --> 00:44:35,130
Like what?

641
00:44:39,218 --> 00:44:43,514
You know, Natalie, if you think
that I had something to do

642
00:44:43,597 --> 00:44:45,307
with your father's death…

643
00:44:47,017 --> 00:44:48,602
you approached the wrong person.

644
00:44:54,566 --> 00:44:57,361
You're so defensive. Fine, I'm sorry.

645
00:44:59,780 --> 00:45:02,991
If I give you what you want…

646
00:45:04,952 --> 00:45:08,205
will you tell me what you know?

647
00:45:10,958 --> 00:45:12,000
Hmm?

648
00:45:30,686 --> 00:45:31,687
[indistinct chatter]

649
00:45:32,187 --> 00:45:34,022
[Diego] Uncle! Uncle!

650
00:45:34,606 --> 00:45:36,817
-Everyone! Nanny!
-[Loring] Oh, Diego!

651
00:45:37,401 --> 00:45:39,278
-[Pandoy] Diego, you're back.
-I missed you, all!

652
00:45:39,361 --> 00:45:41,405
-We missed you too.
-[Diego] Uncle, how are you?

653
00:45:41,488 --> 00:45:42,865
[chuckling]

654
00:45:43,574 --> 00:45:45,200
-[Diego] Mr. Raul.
-How have you been?

655
00:45:47,077 --> 00:45:49,371
Wait, what brings you to the cooperative?

656
00:45:49,455 --> 00:45:51,081
Aside from wanting to see you all,

657
00:45:51,582 --> 00:45:54,084
-I want to introduce someone.
-Who?

658
00:45:56,086 --> 00:45:58,046
[Loring] Oh! Hold on.

659
00:45:58,130 --> 00:46:02,050
Everyone, meet Miss Camia, Lily's mother.

660
00:46:02,134 --> 00:46:03,594
-[Loring] Oh!
-[Fernan] So, that's her.

661
00:46:03,677 --> 00:46:05,637
-Good day to all of you.
-Ma'am Camia,

662
00:46:05,721 --> 00:46:06,972
it's really you.

663
00:46:07,055 --> 00:46:08,015
How are you?

664
00:46:08,098 --> 00:46:13,353
Ma'am, I saw how you condemned
the Ardientes on TV.

665
00:46:13,687 --> 00:46:17,232
I believe that you are telling the truth.

666
00:46:17,316 --> 00:46:19,943
You need to be careful, Miss Camia.

667
00:46:20,027 --> 00:46:22,905
-Please be safe.
-You don't have to worry

668
00:46:22,988 --> 00:46:24,781
because I have my bodyguards.

669
00:46:24,865 --> 00:46:28,827
And besides, Diego is here to protect me.

670
00:46:28,911 --> 00:46:30,621
[man] Yeah, you can count on Diego.

671
00:46:30,704 --> 00:46:31,914
Of course.

672
00:46:31,997 --> 00:46:36,001
[Diego] I came here
to ask for your support.

673
00:46:37,044 --> 00:46:40,797
Let me be your voice in this town.

674
00:46:42,132 --> 00:46:45,093
Yes, you heard it right.

675
00:46:46,428 --> 00:46:49,765
I, Diego Ardiente-Torillo…

676
00:46:50,557 --> 00:46:54,645
will run for governor
in the next election!

677
00:46:55,687 --> 00:46:58,524
[applause]

678
00:46:58,607 --> 00:47:01,485
[farmer] You deserve
to be the governor, Diego.

679
00:47:02,194 --> 00:47:03,570
Since the beginning,

680
00:47:03,654 --> 00:47:06,031
you've known the hardships
of the townspeople.

681
00:47:06,698 --> 00:47:08,700
We support you. Run, Diego!

682
00:47:09,117 --> 00:47:11,078
Run, Diego! Run, Diego!

683
00:47:12,579 --> 00:47:13,830
Go, Diego!

684
00:47:13,914 --> 00:47:15,874
-Fighting!
-We'll fight with you, Diego!

685
00:47:15,958 --> 00:47:17,459
[applause]

686
00:47:17,543 --> 00:47:21,296
[all] Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

687
00:47:22,422 --> 00:47:24,341
[Ivy] You'll run for governor?

688
00:47:26,593 --> 00:47:27,636
Yes.

689
00:47:28,845 --> 00:47:31,723
I'm the mayor of this town,
so the next logical step

690
00:47:31,807 --> 00:47:34,768
is either to be a governor or a senator.

691
00:47:35,686 --> 00:47:38,021
And I figured that
the Ardiente folks need me.

692
00:47:39,606 --> 00:47:43,068
It's not as if someone
will dare to challenge me.

693
00:47:44,778 --> 00:47:46,363
And I want you by my side…

694
00:47:48,824 --> 00:47:50,242
during the organization…

695
00:47:51,493 --> 00:47:52,536
the filing…

696
00:47:53,704 --> 00:47:55,914
and until the campaign starts.

697
00:48:00,586 --> 00:48:03,130
I would love to, Mr. Mayor.

698
00:48:03,547 --> 00:48:04,590
But…

699
00:48:06,466 --> 00:48:12,639
it will only happen if your mom
and grandpa support us.

700
00:48:13,307 --> 00:48:15,267
As I see it,

701
00:48:16,435 --> 00:48:17,686
they're both against me.

702
00:48:18,520 --> 00:48:21,398
Miss Aguas, no one can oppose me.

703
00:48:22,816 --> 00:48:25,027
No one can decide for me.

704
00:48:25,861 --> 00:48:27,821
And once I become the governor,

705
00:48:27,904 --> 00:48:31,366
I will be the most powerful Ardiente.

706
00:48:31,450 --> 00:48:33,201
[suspenseful sting]

707
00:48:33,285 --> 00:48:35,287
Everyone will bow to the king,

708
00:48:36,705 --> 00:48:37,664
and you…

709
00:48:40,542 --> 00:48:42,711
You will be my queen.

710
00:49:24,086 --> 00:49:26,546
[Julio] <i>You're going to finish</i>
<i>what you started.</i>

711
00:49:26,630 --> 00:49:28,006
<i>Another's head in exchange</i>
<i>for yours, Madrigal.</i>

712
00:49:28,090 --> 00:49:30,842
[Jepoy] <i>I'll do everything to protect you.</i>

713
00:49:31,510 --> 00:49:33,345
<i>I need to save Jepoy. Get out of my way.</i>

714
00:49:33,428 --> 00:49:34,680
<i>-Move out!</i>
<i>-Yes, he's your friend,</i>

715
00:49:34,763 --> 00:49:35,806
<i>but I love you!</i>

716
00:49:36,431 --> 00:49:39,267
<i>Trust me, Ivy. I'll save Jepoy.</i>

717
00:49:39,601 --> 00:49:41,061
<i>I'll bring him back in one piece.</i>

718
00:49:41,144 --> 00:49:42,688
-[Diego] <i>Jepoy, it's me, Diego.</i>
-[grunting]

719
00:49:42,771 --> 00:49:44,272
<i>Ma'am, I've got the files</i>
<i>that you asked for</i>

720
00:49:44,356 --> 00:49:45,941
<i>from the private investigator.</i>

721
00:49:46,441 --> 00:49:48,694
[Emilia] <i>I won't allow my son to be used</i>

722
00:49:48,777 --> 00:49:51,988
<i>by someone who could betray our family.</i>

723
00:49:52,072 --> 00:49:54,866
-<i>What if I kill you right here?</i>
-[Emilia grunts]

724
00:49:54,950 --> 00:49:56,618
-[Arnaldo] <i>Ivy! Stop this!</i>
-[Ivy] <i>Hands off me!</i>

725
00:49:56,702 --> 00:50:00,038
[theme music playing]
